   "design": "When a ward sets or lifts isolation in the electronic health record ({OTHER}), the cleaning task app ({OPS_SYSTEM}) gets a task with only the room and isolation type, never the diagnosis, so no phone call is needed. The supervisor records the check of each isolation clean with a tap. Assigning, instructing, checking and reporting stay in person.",
   "previous_blocker": "Isolation notices came by phone and cleans were logged on paper.",
   "enabler_now": "Hospital records can pass room-level status to task apps.",
   "still_hard": "Late notices still come by phone; protocols must be followed step by step in the room, not in the app.",
   "human_edge": "Seeing a cleaner take off gloves in the wrong order and stopping them.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Nothing changes.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "infection prevention nurse",
     "task": "Audit isolation cleaning",
     "learn": "Whether tapped records make audits faster."
    }
   ],
   "build_days": {
